{
  "name": "pulling a grandchild up under its grandparent is accepted",
  "notes": "The accepting twin of the cycle refusal, and the staging is load-bearing: the ticket moves under a parent that ITSELF has a parent, so the ancestor walk runs a second iteration instead of stopping at a root. A three-deep chain is not enough for that — moving a grandchild under the ROOT grandparent walks exactly once, and a walk that refused any move whose parent has a parent would still be accepted. Here TKD moves under TKB, whose parent is TKA, so the walk visits TKB then TKA then stops. Two mutations die on this that a root destination survives: refusing when the cursor has a parent, and refusing on entering a second iteration.",
